PyDoc_STRVAR(__pyx_doc_20thorlabs_power_meter_5TLPMX_72setThermopilePulseIntegrator, "\n\t\tEnables or disables thermopile pulse energy measurement. This mode is suitable for measuring the energy in joules from single thermopile pulses with a slow repetition rate. The algorithm integrates the power measurement over a duration of 8 * Tau, where Tau is a sensor-specific time constant stored in the head\047s EEPROM.\n\t\t\n\t\tNotes:\n\t\t(1) Note: The function is only available on powermeters with Thermopile sensor support.\n\t\t(2) For adapter sensors Tau must be specified by setAcclTau function previously\n\t\t\n\t\tArgs:\n\t\t\tenable(c_int16) : True to enable the pulse energy measurement. False to disable it.\n\t\t\tchannel(c_uint16) : Number of the sensor channel. \n\t\t\t\n\t\t\tDefault: 1 for non multi channel devices\n\t\tReturns:\n\t\t\tint: The return value, 0 is for success\n\t\t");
